1
00:04:13,333 --> 00:04:19,333
Live. Die. Repeat.

2
00:08:26,666 --> 00:08:32,666
Edge of Tomorrow is a action, science fiction film directed by Doug Liman.

3
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Major Bill Cage is an officer who has never seen a day of combat when
he is unceremoniously demoted and dropped into combat.

4
00:16:53,333 --> 00:16:59,333
Cage is killed within minutes, managing to take an alpha alien down with him.

5
00:21:06,666 --> 00:21:12,666
He awakens back at the beginning of the same day and
is forced to fight and die again...

6
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:26,000
and again - as physical contact with the alien has thrown him into a time loop.

7
00:29:33,333 --> 00:29:39,333
Cage, played by Tom Cruise.

8
00:33:46,666 --> 00:33:52,666
Rita, played by Emily Blunt.

9
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
General Brigham, played by Brendan Gleeson.

10
00:42:13,333 --> 00:42:19,333
Master Sergeant Farell, played by Bill Paxton.

11
00:46:26,666 --> 00:46:32,666
Skinner, played by Jonas Armstrong.

12
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:46,000
Kimmel, played by Tony Way.

13
00:54:53,333 --> 00:54:59,333
Edge of Tomorrow is a 2014 American science fiction action
film starring Tom Cruise and Emily Blunt.

14
00:59:06,666 --> 00:59:12,666
Directed by Doug Liman and written by Christopher McQuarrie, Jez Butterworth and John-Henry
Butterworth, it is based on the Japanese light novel All You Need Is Kill by Hiroshi Sakurazaka.

15
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
The film takes place in a future where most of Europe is
occupied by an alien race known as mimics.

16
01:07:33,333 --> 01:07:39,333
Major William Cage (Cruise), a public relations officer with no combat experience, is forced by his superiors to join a landing
operation against the aliens, only to find himself experiencing a time loop as he tries to find a way to defeat the mimics.

17
01:11:46,666 --> 01:11:52,666
Bill Paxton and Brendan Gleeson appear in supporting roles.

18
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
In late 2009, 3 Arts Entertainment purchased the rights to All You
Need Is Kill and sold the spec script to Warner Bros.

19
01:20:13,333 --> 01:20:19,333
The studio produced Edge of Tomorrow with the involvement of 3 Arts, the novel's
publisher Viz Media, and Australian production company Village Roadshow.

20
01:24:26,666 --> 01:24:32,666
Filming began in late 2012, taking place in England: at Warner Bros.

21
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
Studios in Leavesden, outside London, and other locations, such as
London's Trafalgar Square and the coastal Saunton Sands.

22
01:32:53,333 --> 01:32:59,333
A total of nine companies handled the visual effects.

23
01:37:06,666 --> 01:37:12,666
Edge of Tomorrow was released theatrically in select territories on
May 30, 2014, and in the United States on June 6.

24
01:41:20,000 --> 01:41:26,000
The film received positive reviews from critics, and grossed
$370 million against a $178 million budget.

25
01:45:33,333 --> 01:45:39,333
The film explores themes of deja vu, based on novel or
book, restart, military officer, dystopia.

26
01:49:46,666 --> 01:49:52,666
The tone is thought_provoking.
